# The city where I was born in Russian: город, где…
subtitle: "Город, где я родился; деревня, куда мы ездили; Казань, откуда он приезжал: где, куда and откуда after a noun in Russian."
tags: ["russian","relative clauses","где куда откуда","kazan","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/relative-clauses","vocabulary/family"]
thumb: "band \"The village where I grew up\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Something for you in Russian: кое-что, что-то, что-нибудь","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/163-russian-someone-something.cast"}

