audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    '|a||The city where I was born in Russian: город, где…':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Город, где я родился; деревня, куда мы ездили; Казань, откуда он приезжал: где, куда and откуда after a noun in Russian.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:15fv5cd'
    '|a||А́вгуст. В «Неве́» ти́хий день.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3720
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Мы с Со́фьей се́ли пить чай. Послу́шайте.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:p0u9yg'
    '|a||Со́фья, ты ведь из Каза́ни?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:13zm97z'
    '|b||Да, Каза́нь — мой родно́й го́род. Но я вы́росла в дере́вне, где жила́ моя́ тётя.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5440
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||А где э́та дере́вня?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1520
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Недалеко́, к ю́гу от Каза́ни. Там большо́й сад, куда́ мы ходи́ли ка́ждое у́тро.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||А дя́дя?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1680
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|b||Дя́дя рабо́тал в Каза́ни, отку́да он приезжа́л к нам ка́ждую суббо́ту.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4280
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Where did Софья grow up? (вы́росла: grew up; дере́вня: village)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||В дере́вне, где жила́ тётя.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2520
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||What was there in the village? (сад: garden)':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Большо́й сад.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 1480
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||How often did her uncle (дя́дя) come?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Ка́ждую суббо́ту, из Каза́ни.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Посмотри́те. Со́фья сказа́ла: я вы́росла в дере́вне, где жила́ тётя.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5080
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Вы́расти: to grow up. Он вы́рос, она́ вы́росла.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:150g6qz'
    '|a||Где here asks nothing: it joins the two halves, like кото́рый, which you know from lesson 131.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:16qn9e8'
    '|a||Дере́вня, где жила́ тётя: дере́вня, в кото́рой жила́ тётя.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1eh1qzc'
    '|a||Где, куда́, отку́да: each one stands for a кото́рый.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:ygbyjl'
    '|a||Дере́вня, где жила́ тётя: в кото́рой. Где? The in-colour.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:196zg06'
    '|a||Сад, куда́ мы ходи́ли: в кото́рый. Куда́? The object colour. Сад is a garden.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1089cbi'
    '|a||Каза́нь, отку́да он приезжа́л: из кото́рой. Отку́да? The of-colour.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ckipuw'
    '|a||Mostly after a place. After a person, only кото́рый: челове́к, кото́рый.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:yqbfet'
    '|a||Со́фья сказа́ла: Каза́нь — мой родно́й го́род. Родно́й го́род: your home town,':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:d9j5hk'
    '|a||го́род, где родила́сь Со́фья.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fp8dcm'
    '|a||Дя́дя, uncle, and тётя, aunt. Дя́дя ends in я, but he takes мой: мой дя́дя.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1rrdsn9'
    '|a||Сад, a garden; in the garden, в саду́, like на полу́. And у́гол, a corner: на углу́, on the corner.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1fjqtdu'
    '|a||А где дере́вня? Се́вер,':
